WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.783
Ask for a testimonial after a first win, not after silence.

00:00:03.783 --> 00:00:06.534
This lesson is about ask for a testimonial.

00:00:06.534 --> 00:00:07.566
After first win.

00:00:07.566 --> 00:00:09.973
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:09.973 --> 00:00:13.412
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:13.412 --> 00:00:18.570
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:22.353
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:22.353 --> 00:00:26.136
Stay practical: draft ask template before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:26.456 --> 00:00:28.631
Wait until they felt a result.

00:00:28.631 --> 00:00:31.169
Then ask while the win is fresh.

00:00:31.169 --> 00:00:33.344
Remember the objective: draft ask template.

00:00:33.344 --> 00:00:37.332
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:37.332 --> 00:00:41.682
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:41.682 --> 00:00:45.670
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:50.020
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:52.558
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:00:52.558 --> 00:00:54.008
Feedback beats guessing alone.

00:00:54.328 --> 00:00:59.407
Draft an ask template with two prompts: what changed, and would you recommend it.

